<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIA YIELD SPREADS-U.S. CASTS CLOUD OVER BLOC.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIA YIELD SPREADS-U.S. CASTS CLOUD OVER BLOC.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> AUD VS   3-YR	   10-YR	* AUD 3-YR/10-YR SPREAD</p>
<p> USD	-49 (+ 01)    35 (+ 07) * FUTURES   82   (+ 05.5)</p>
<p> CAD	 59 (- 01)    61 (+ 07) * CASH	102  (+ 06)</p>
<p> NZD     -176 (- 06)   -42 (- 01) *</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Australian bond market underperformed against both U.S. and Canadian debt in anticipation of a further sell-off in U.S. Treasuries on Friday.</p>
<p>While the local market has shown an outperforming bias against the U.S. for most of the week on a positive fundamental basis, the weight of depression in the U.S. is also beginning to taint favourable technicals, analysts said.</p>
<p>However, local debt once again outshone the New Zealand market which was weighed down by continued weakness in the N.Z. dollar.</p>
<p>-- Colin Brinsden 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
